[Music]  when it comes to unlocking all the  benefits of the cloud  you don't want identity and access  management to get in the way  users from your company can use their  existing accounts to access your  company's google cloud environment by  signing in with their credentials  and you can manage which permissions  these users have with identity and  access management  or iam for short  but when users who use a different  identity provider need access things  aren't so simple  using an external identity provider can  make getting access complicated and get  in the way of doing the work that really  matters  so how can you provide your employees  partners contractors and everyone else  with a secure way to access your  environment and resources  workforce identity federation lets you  use an external identity provider to  directly authenticate users into your  google cloud environment  now you have even more control for how  users can sign into and access google  cloud services  with workforce identity federation  you don't need to synchronize user  identities from your existing identity  provider into google cloud  instead  users will be able to authenticate with  their existing credentials in a single  sign-on flow let's take a closer look at  how it works  first the user can sign in through a  typical login flow this can include the  interface offered by your identity  provider the interface from your service  provider such as google cloud or by  using the apis or command line interface  all of these will use your identity  provider's information to authenticate  the user and will return a response  validating the user  then  the valid response is sent to workforce  identity federation where the token is  validated against the rules that you've  set up  a new google cloud token will be  generated that contains the  authorization for this user  finally the user can be redirected to  the console using the new login token  now you've ensured that only legitimate  users have access to authorized  resources with a frictionless sign-on  experience and you don't need to manage  syncing up identities between providers  in order for a user to sign in with  workforce identity federation  you'll first need to set it up for your  google cloud organization  this setup process involves two steps  first  you'll need to set up one or more  workforce pools  these pools let you manage and group  together users  and control their access to your google  cloud environment  you can customize the identity and  access management permissions for each  pool  so you can follow the best practice of  least privilege and ensure that users  only have the permissions they need  in addition to setting im permissions  for an entire pool  you can also set permissions for  individual users or subgroups of a pool  based on attributes from your identity  provider  once you've created your workforce pools  you'll need to create a workforce  identity pool provider for each pool  these pool providers store the  information for your identity provider  as well as the mapping for attributes  you can also customize how attributes  are mapped from your identity provider  so you only need to include the  necessary details and protect your users  data  pools can be mapped to a group of users  using these attributes such as  separating employees from partners  with the workforce pool and workforce  pool provider setup users can seamlessly  sign in and access your google cloud  resources  to learn more about how workforce  identity federation can help you manage  access to your google cloud environment  check out the documentation and try it  out for yourself

